"missing_conditions": [{"part": 1, "text": "The source's point applies only to participatory research, and it concerns methods that may deviate from classical approaches, not the amount of time required.", "quote": "In research that is participatory, the investigator learns to develop methods for assuring internal validity that may deviate from classical approaches"}, {"part": 2, "text": "The source concerns developing methods in participatory research and redefining required skills, not additional development time; the claim omits the participatory and skills-based scope.", "quote": "the movement towards multiple, complex, and community-based interventions has implications for redefining the types of skills required to research and practice community public health approaches"}, {"part": 3, "text": "The source's implementation impediments apply to complex community programs and concern reaching planned targets at the correct time, not additional implementation time for multiple approaches.", "quote": "Flay (1986) focused on the impediments in implementing complex community programs, including reaching the planned targets at the correct time"}]}

